teslamate-rs for Debian
-----------------------

Data directory
  SQLite lives at /srv/teslamate-rs/teslamate-rs.sqlite (WAL files alongside).
  Removing the package does not delete that directory.

Service
  systemd unit teslamate-rs.service binds 127.0.0.1:4010 and does not start
  the Tesla Owner API logger until tokens are stored (teslamate-rs login).
  Override bind/port/database in /etc/default/teslamate-rs.

  PAM password checks use a socket-activated one-shot helper running with
  group shadow. The long-lived web daemon is not a member of shadow and
  retains NoNewPrivileges=yes. On upgrades, postinst removes the old shadow
  group membership before restarting the service.

  This package is meant to sit beside Docker TeslaMate (port 4000), not
  replace it.

Build
  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b -d
  Requires rustc 1.98.1 (rust-toolchain.toml). rustup's cargo is used when
  ~/.cargo/bin is on PATH; -d skips the apt cargo/rustc build-depends.
